# AgentPulse — environment.
#
# Copy to .env and edit, or run ./install.sh, which resolves most of this for
# you. NEVER commit .env — it holds the shared secret.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Tags — read by the installer, ignored by compose and the services.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Every variable has exactly one tag line directly above it, and a line is a
# variable only if it has one. `VAR=` is set by default; `# VAR=` exists but is
# unset by default. Prose lines that merely look like assignments are ignored.
#
#   @required   must resolve to a non-empty value, or the install stops
#   @optional   may stay unset; the service's own default applies
#   @secret     never echoed, logged or passed as an argument; masked in output
#   @generated  created by the installer if unset (openssl rand -hex 32),
#               never regenerated once set
#   @derived    computed from other variables; never prompted for
#   @detect     auto-detected on this machine, then confirmed
#   @prompt     asked for when nothing else resolves it
#   @docker     only meaningful in Docker mode
#   @native     only meaningful in native (no Docker) mode
#
# A variable with neither @docker nor @native applies to both.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Database
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# @optional
POSTGRES_USER=aiuo
# The value below is a placeholder and counts as unset.
# @required @secret @generated
POSTGRES_PASSWORD=change-me-before-first-run
# @optional
POSTGRES_DB=aiuo

# In-compose connection string. Services reach postgres over the compose
# network on port 5432 — never through the published host port. Compose builds
# its own from the three values above and ignores this one; a native install
# reads it directly (migrate, collector, proxy and web all require it).
# @required @secret @derived @native
DATABASE_URL=postgres://aiuo:change-me-before-first-run@postgres:5432/aiuo

# Published host ports. All bound to 127.0.0.1 in compose, never 0.0.0.0.
# Change any that collide with something already on this machine — a native
# postgres, another project's dev server. Only the host side moves; services
# still reach each other on the compose network at the container port.
# In native mode these are the ports the services themselves listen on.
# @optional @detect
POSTGRES_HOST_PORT=5433
# @optional @detect
COLLECTOR_HOST_PORT=4317
# @optional @detect
PROXY_HOST_PORT=4318
# @optional @detect
WEB_HOST_PORT=3000

# From the host (psql, the migrate runner run locally). Must match
# POSTGRES_HOST_PORT above. Read by no service — it is for you.
# @optional @secret @derived
DATABASE_URL_HOST=postgres://aiuo:change-me-before-first-run@127.0.0.1:5433/aiuo

# Compose pins TZ=UTC in every container regardless of this value, and native
# units do the same. Kept so a host-side tool sourcing .env agrees.
# @optional
TZ=UTC

# Build args for the collector image. Must match your host user or git rejects
# the bind-mounted repos with "detected dubious ownership". `make uid` prints
# them.
# @optional @detect @docker
# HOST_UID=501
# @optional @detect @docker
# HOST_GID=20

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Redaction — runs BEFORE insert, over prompts, responses, command output and
# diff bodies alike. Version is stamped on every content row.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The pattern set is compiled in, at packages/schema/src/redaction.ts. There is
# no file to point at: an earlier REDACTION_PATTERNS_FILE line here was read by
# nothing, so editing the file it named would have changed no behaviour while
# looking like it had.
#
# To change the patterns, edit that module AND bump Redactor.version. Each row
# records the version it was written under, and that is only an audit trail if
# one version means one pattern set forever. Both services now refuse to start
# if a version already in the database has a different pattern hash.
#
# Escape hatch for debugging only. With this true the collector writes rows at
# redaction_version 0, which means raw secrets land in the database.
# @optional
REDACTION_DISABLED=false

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Ingest caps
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# @optional
COLLECTOR_MAX_STDOUT_BYTES=8192
# @optional
COLLECTOR_MAX_DIFF_BYTES=262144
# @optional
COLLECTOR_MAX_TURN_DIFF_BYTES=2097152

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Proxy (Layer 3). Point an agent here with its base-URL env var:
#   export ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:4318
# For several upstreams at once, use the /_u/<name>/ prefix routes below.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# @optional
PROXY_DEFAULT_UPSTREAM=https://api.anthropic.com
# @optional
# PROXY_UPSTREAMS=openai=https://api.openai.com,openrouter=https://openrouter.ai/api,ollama=http://host.docker.internal:11434
# @optional
PROXY_MAX_STORED_BODY_BYTES=65536
# Largest request/response body forwarded, and how much of a response is
# buffered for usage extraction. Compose does not pass these; native does.
# @optional @native
# PROXY_MAX_BODY_BYTES=33554432
# @optional @native
# PROXY_MAX_CAPTURE_BYTES=8388608

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Collector / web. PATH_MAP and friends are read by the collector today.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Ordered host_prefix:container_prefix pairs, comma separated. Applied inbound
# (hook events carry host paths) and outbound (the DB stores host paths).
#
# MUST cover the agent home as well as the code roots. Checkpoints are keyed on
# each transcript's HOST path and the database rejects /host/... outright, so a
# missing agent-home entry means every transcript fails to checkpoint. The
# collector asserts this at startup.
#
# Code roots: CODE_ROOT_1 is mounted by compose.yaml; CODE_ROOT_2, _3, … are
# mounted by compose.override.yaml, which `make compose-override` generates
# from this file (make up/web/dev run it). Each needs a PATH_MAP entry
# targeting /host/code/rootN.
#
# In native mode there is no /host layer: every entry is an identity mapping
# (host path on both sides), most specific prefix first.
#
# @optional @detect
# CLAUDE_HOME=/Users/you/.claude
# @optional @detect
# GEMINI_HOME=/Users/you/.gemini
# @required @prompt
# CODE_ROOT_1=/Volumes/disk/Projects
# @optional @prompt
# CODE_ROOT_2=/Volumes/disk/Practice
# @required @derived
# PATH_MAP=/Users/you/.claude:/host/agents/claude,/Users/you/.gemini:/host/agents/gemini,/Volumes/disk/Projects:/host/code/root1,/Volumes/disk/Practice:/host/code/root2
# @optional @detect
# WATCH_MODE=auto
# @optional
# WATCH_POLL_INTERVAL_MS=2000
# At least 16 characters. Also baked into ~/.claude/aiuo/post-event.sh by
# `make install-hooks`, so changing it means re-running that.
# @required @secret @generated
# COLLECTOR_SHARED_SECRET=
# @optional @detect
# AGENT_CLAUDE_CODE_ENABLED=true
# The four below have no adapter yet; enabling one only logs a warning.
# @optional
# AGENT_CODEX_CLI_ENABLED=false
# @optional
# AGENT_QWEN_CODE_ENABLED=false
# @optional
# AGENT_CURSOR_CLI_ENABLED=false
# @optional
# AGENT_COPILOT_CLI_ENABLED=false
# Compose defaults this to true when unset, the collector to false. Set it
# explicitly.
# @optional @detect
# AGENT_GEMINI_CLI_ENABLED=false
# @optional @native
# LOG_LEVEL=info

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Native mode only — compose hard-codes all of these.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Where the collector reads each agent's state. In compose these are the
# /host/agents/* mount targets; natively they are the host directories.
# @derived @native
# AGENT_CLAUDE_CODE_HOME=/Users/you/.claude
# @derived @native
# AGENT_GEMINI_CLI_HOME=/Users/you/.gemini
# @derived @native
# AGENT_CODEX_CLI_HOME=
# @derived @native
# AGENT_QWEN_CODE_HOME=
# @derived @native
# AGENT_CURSOR_CLI_HOME=
# @derived @native
# AGENT_COPILOT_CLI_HOME=
#
# Listen ports — equal to the *_HOST_PORT values above natively.
# @derived @native
# COLLECTOR_PORT=4317
# @derived @native
# PROXY_PORT=4318
#
# Listen addresses. The services default to 0.0.0.0, which is right inside a
# container that publishes 127.0.0.1 only. Natively nothing sits in front of
# them, so these must be 127.0.0.1 or your history is reachable from the LAN.
# @derived @native
# COLLECTOR_BIND_HOST=127.0.0.1
# @derived @native
# PROXY_BIND_HOST=127.0.0.1
#
# The dashboard's bind address and port are Next.js's own HOSTNAME and PORT.
# The native web unit sets them from WEB_HOST_PORT (HOSTNAME=127.0.0.1); they
# are deliberately not read from this file, because HOSTNAME is a common
# shell variable.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Dashboard — compaction
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The compact panel folds a hand-picked run of turns into one context block.
# Assembly is local and always works: the block is built from the database by
# apps/web/src/lib/compact.ts, with no network call.
#
# Setting a key adds an optional second step — handing that block to Claude to
# summarise. It is the ONLY outbound request the dashboard makes, it happens
# only when someone presses "Compact turns", and the panel states on every
# result whether a model ran and which one answered. Each press is a billed API
# call against this key.
#
# Leave it unset and the panel returns the assembled record itself, labelled as
# such. Nothing else in the stack changes.
#
# @optional @secret @prompt
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# The local alternative. Ollama runs the model on this machine, so a compaction
# keeps the property the rest of the stack has: nothing leaves the host. The
# panel lists whatever models the daemon reports and marks each one local or
# remote — a `:cloud` model is proxied through ollama.com and DOES leave.
#
# Start the daemon with `ollama serve`; pull a model with e.g.
# `ollama pull qwen2.5-coder`. Nothing needs to be set here for the default.
#
# Beware the reason the code checks context windows: Ollama does not refuse an
# over-long prompt, it drops the overflow and returns success. Verified on this
# machine 2026-09-23 (Ollama 0.34.2) — 4,600 tokens in, 258 evaluated, a
# confident wrong answer out. The panel refuses the run instead.
#
# From the host, the default is right. In compose the container cannot reach the
# host's loopback, so compose.yaml points it at host.docker.internal instead.
#
# @optional @detect
# OLLAMA_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:11434

# Compact history. Each compaction run from a turn's detail page is stored with
# the settings that produced it, because the same turn at 'brief' with prompts
# only and at 'detailed' with diffs gives two documents that look equally
# authoritative and say very different amounts.
#
# The dashboard does NOT write this. Its pool is read-only and stays that way —
# it POSTs to the collector, which inserts. So the dashboard needs the same
# shared secret the hook script uses, and a way to reach the collector. In
# compose both are set for you (COLLECTOR_URL=http://collector:4317); these two
# matter only when running `next dev` on the host.
#
# Without the secret, compacting still works and still shows its result — the
# panel just says it was not saved, rather than pretending it was.
#
# @derived @native
# COLLECTOR_URL=http://127.0.0.1:4317

# Decorative: initials shown in the dashboard header. Compose does not pass it
# to the web container, so today it only takes effect natively.
# @optional @native
# AIUO_OPERATOR=
